<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3180] Subsequent save operation on interpreter add whitespace to permissions</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3180</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The zeppelin-web adds whitespaces on permissions, when saving interpreting settings the second time after permissions were added.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So when adding permissions, the initial save operation works fine.&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
 e.g.&#160; owners:&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;&amp;quot;admin&amp;quot;&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&#160;is defined and send to the server.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But when invoking subsequent save operations without modifying the permissions, then the invalid whitespace is added to the permissions: owners:&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;&amp;quot;admin &amp;quot;&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
